    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "ok, cool. lets try something technical. i need you to look at a simple loop in python that's processing a massive list of integers to find primes. i want you to tell me how to optimize it. keep the answer brief and don't go into anything crazy like distributed computing or complex math libraries, just standard single-threaded optimizations. \n\n```python\ndef find_primes(n):\n    primes = []\n    for i in range(2, n):\n        is_prime = True\n        for j in range(2, i):\n            if i % j == 0:\n                is_prime = False\n                break\n        if is_prime:\n            primes.append(i)\n    return primes\n```\n\njust give me the most straightforward way to make this faster without making the code look too complicated.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
